# VibeSafe — Cursor Rules

Read VIBESAFE_PRD.md fully before making any decision.

Tech stack: Node.js 18+, TypeScript strict mode, pnpm workspaces, Turborepo, commander.js, chalk, boxen, ora, vitest, tsup.

## Coding Rules

- Never use `any` type. Always use the types defined in src/types.ts
- All async functions must handle errors explicitly (no unhandled promise rejections)
- All terminal output goes through src/output/ — never console.log directly in scanners
- Comments explain WHY not WHAT
- Every exported function needs a JSDoc comment

## Build Order

Follow the Cursor Prompting Plan in Section 14 of VIBESAFE_PRD.md. Build in order:

1. Prompt 0 — Project setup (monorepo + CLI scaffold)
2. Prompt 1 — Project type detection + ignore patterns
3. Prompt 2 — Secrets scanner
4. Prompt 3 — Dependency scanner
5. Prompt 4 — SAST with Semgrep
6. Prompt 5 — Safety Score + Terminal output
7. Prompt 6 — LLM fix engine
8. Prompt 7 — GitHub PR creation

Do not skip ahead. Each prompt builds on the last.
